{
 "title": "HashMap y HashSet",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "`std.collections` ofrece el diccionario clave → valor **`HashMap[K, V]`** y el conjunto sin repetidos **`HashSet[K]`**. `hashmap_new[K, V]()` crea un diccionario vacío; `insert` añade, `get` devuelve un `Optional`, `get_or` da un valor por defecto, `contains` pregunta si existe una clave y `len` dice cuántas hay."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.collections",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    ages = collections.hashmap_new[str, i32]()",
    "    ages.insert(\"ali\", 30)",
    "    ages.insert(\"ayse\", 25)",
    "    print(ages.len())",
    "    print(ages.get_or(\"ali\", 0))",
    "    print(ages.contains(\"zeynep\"))",
    "    match ages.get(\"ayse\"):",
    "        Valid(a):",
    "            print(\"ayse is\", a)",
    "        None:",
    "            print(\"not found\")"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "2",
    "30",
    "false",
    "ayse is 25"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.collections",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    seen = collections.hashset_new[i32]()",
    "    print(seen.insert(3))",
    "    print(seen.insert(7))",
    "    print(seen.insert(3))",
    "    print(seen.len(), seen.contains(7))"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "true",
    "true",
    "false",
    "2 true"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "`HashSet.insert` devuelve `true` si la clave era nueva y `false` si ya estaba; es útil para encontrar repetidos."
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c10-l03-x1",
   "prompt": "Cuenta cuántas veces aparece cada una de las palabras `\"a\"`, `\"b\"`, `\"a\"`, `\"c\"`, `\"b\"`, `\"a\"` usando un `HashMap[str, i32]` e imprime el contador de `\"a\"`.",
   "starter": [
    "import std.collections",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    words: [6]str = [\"a\", \"b\", \"a\", \"c\", \"b\", \"a\"]",
    "    counts = collections.hashmap_new[str, i32]()",
    "    print(counts.get_or(\"a\", 0))"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "import std.collections",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    words: [6]str = [\"a\", \"b\", \"a\", \"c\", \"b\", \"a\"]",
    "    counts = collections.hashmap_new[str, i32]()",
    "    for w in words:",
    "        counts.insert(w, counts.get_or(w, 0) + 1)",
    "    print(counts.get_or(\"a\", 0))"
   ],
   "hint": "Para cada palabra haz `counts.insert(w, counts.get_or(w, 0) + 1)`.",
   "expected": [
    "3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c10-l03-q1",
   "q": "¿Qué da `get_or(key, 0)` cuando falta la clave?",
   "options": [
    "Un error",
    "0 (el valor por defecto dado)",
    "`None`"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`get_or` recibe un valor por defecto; `get` devuelve un `Optional`."
  }
 ]
}
